course: dictionary
lesson: 15222
title: Serviceable and faint praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can describe something that is good in a plain, useful way without being special. Serviceable is one of those words. It means good enough to be used, working well, even if it is not new or beautiful. «My old bike is still serviceable, so I ride it to school every day.» The bike is not shiny, but it works, so it is serviceable.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Ask yourself: does the thing work, and is it special? «The serviceable shoes were strong and practical for muddy walks.» Strong and practical are clues that serviceable means useful and made to last.
explain: Sometimes people use serviceable as faint praise. «The school play was a serviceable performance.» That does not sound thrilled. It means the play was good enough, but not special. Try your meaning in the sentence, "good enough, but not special", and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Serviceable means good enough to be used, working well even if it is not new or beautiful.
fact: «Serviceable shoes» are strong and practical, made to last.
fact: Something serviceable can be repaired or serviced, so it can stay in use.
fact: When praise is faint, "serviceable" means good enough rather than excellent: «a serviceable performance» is not a great performance.
fact: The phrases «in serviceable condition» and «perfectly serviceable» both mean that a thing works properly.
exercise: «My old bike is still serviceable, so I ride it every day.» What does serviceable mean here? | Very expensive | Brand new and shiny | * Good enough to use and working well | Too broken to repair
exercise: «The school play was a serviceable performance.» What does this suggest about the play? | It was cancelled before it started | It was very loud and funny | * It was good enough, but not especially special | It was the best play anyone had ever seen
exercise: «The serviceable shoes were strong and practical for muddy walks.» Which words show what serviceable means here? | Shoes were | For muddy | Muddy walks | * Strong and practical
test: «The old radio is in serviceable condition, so we can still listen to it.» What does in serviceable condition mean? | * It works properly | It is covered in paint | It has never been used | It is for sale in a shop
test: «Dad said the old tent was perfectly serviceable for one more camping trip.» What does perfectly serviceable mean? | It is brand new | It is too big to fit in the car | * It is good enough to use | It is made of gold
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to serviceable? | Brilliant | Gigantic | Fancy | * Usable
